/-
We define the concept of interface mutants for composed programs and prove that the composition gap γ is bounded by the number of interface mutants.

We first define `Program`, `kills`, `is_test_suite`, and `kappa` (the size of the smallest test suite).
We then define `Program.comp` and `gamma` (the complexity of the extra mutants in a composition).
We prove several lemmas about `kappa` and `gamma`, including `kappa_union`, `kappa_subset`, and bounds related to surjectivity and injectivity.
We define `InterfaceMutants` as the set of mutants in the composed system that are not equivalent to any mutant of the individual components.
Finally, we prove `gamma_le_interface_mutants_card`, which states that γ is less than or equal to the number of interface mutants, provided the set of interface mutants is finite. This formalizes the statement "The composition gap is bounded by the number of interface mutants."
-/

